=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# play environment/kept ----------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode, mocks: the Environment screen proposed for slice 9,$
# drawn from the Environment control's reading of a simulated$
# host (environment.Read), each change the control's on the real$
# plan/apply engine (steps.Sudoers). The screen is the$
# gallery's, unit (c)'s to build. Nothing on this machine$
# changes: every command and file is the fake's, and its record$
# is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: environment/kept$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13, sudo 1.9.16p2. hardn's$
# /etc/sudoers.d/hardn-env-alice keeps HARDN_CONFIG; alice ran$
# sudo hardn; it kept /home/alice/hardn.yml.$
$
# Environment Variable Settings ################################$
$
# HARDN_CONFIG -------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  User                 alice$
  [+] Under sudo           Kept$
   -  Value                /home/alice/hardn.yml$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Under sudo           Stop keeping HARDN_CONFIG$
   2) Guide                How to set HARDN_CONFIG$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-2 or q]: 1$
$
# Stop Keeping HARDN_CONFIG ####################################$
$
# HARDN_CONFIG -------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  User                 alice$
  [ ] Under sudo           Not kept$
$
   -  Stop keeping HARDN_CONFIG$
      /etc/sudoers.d/hardn-env-alice$
      @@ -1,2 +0,0 @@$
      -# Managed by hardn$
      -Defaults:alice env_keep += "HARDN_CONFIG"$
$
  Stop keeping HARDN_CONFIG under sudo? [y/N, 0 or q]: y$
$
  [+] Stop keeping HARDN_CONFIG  Done$
$
# Operation Successful$
$
  Backup of /etc/sudoers.d/hardn-env-alice kept in$
  /var/backups/hardn/20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx$
$
  Takes effect at the next sudo hardn.$
$
# Environment Variable Settings ################################$
$
# HARDN_CONFIG -------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  User                 alice$
  [ ] Under sudo           Not kept$
   -  Value                /home/alice/hardn.yml$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Under sudo           Keep HARDN_CONFIG$
   2) Guide                How to set HARDN_CONFIG$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-2 or q]: 0$
$
# simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Info: environment/kept$
# Recorded by the fake, not done: what each step ran on web-$
# 01.example.net, and the files it changed, in order; hardn's$
# own journal, run directory and backups left out.$
$
   -  Applied: Stop keeping HARDN_CONFIG$
      /etc/sudoers.d/hardn-env-alice$
$

